#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:5
#: 83c749418f91419da11bf87e46386347
msgid "Submitting Patches Back to Master"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:10
#: 7670244b3af24c26bdf66e53b1c36a97
msgid "*Before* working on a new patch search for existing related pull requests, and check for linked pull requests in the issue you're planning to fix. If someone is already working on the problem you can review/test their submission and join the discussion thread instead of creating your own submission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:12
#: 06117d5781a343d78f616bc845e5ff47
msgid "Once you have a bug fix or new feature you would like to have included in the ArduPilot project you should submit a `Pull Request <https://help.github.com/articles/about-pull-requests/>`__. The main developers will see your changes in the `Pulls list, <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/pulls>`__ review them and if all goes well they will be merged into master."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:17
#: 443cc6ff1e5c4dccaf89f227c5302c8e
msgid "This page provides advice to make the process go smoothly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:20
#: f308f2e414b94f69bf0b98ec2cc907bb
msgid "Preparing commits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:22
#: 2059b4d7af7a467485b8e412a6045123
msgid "Commits should be **in a new branch** of your :ref:`fork <git-fork>`/:ref:`clone <git-clone>` (i.e. not \"master\"). These should be done on a local branch and then pushed to your web-based fork of ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:24
#: 1d05b8128b714ce481f2ce1ec613e05d
msgid "The new branch should be :ref:`up-to-date <git-rebase>` with `ArduPilot/master <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot>`__  and should not include any other changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:26
#: fcac955412f34930be115ea9e51c17e9
msgid "**Commits should be small and do just one thing.** If a change touches multiple libraries then there should be a separate commit per library, and a separate commit per vehicle directory. This is true even if it means that intermediate commits break the build. This also implies that moving code from one library to another happens in two commits: one that \"deletes\" it from the old spot, and a separate one that \"creates\" it at the new spot. It's better for unrelated changes in a single library to be separate commits in the pull request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:35
#: 16c16bf9f964409e8cdea7411149cc1b
msgid "Do not create 'only fix formatting' commits. The disruption they cause to git history is more significant than their improvement to the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:38
#: 2cc6ef26eb884915b83a8dbe533537a6
msgid "Only add \"high value\" comments to existing code. Comments disrupt the git history, and the code should already be written clearly enough to describe what it does. Be prepared to explain/defend the importance of any new comments to reviewers, and defer to their judgement to resolve any disagreement over a comment's value. Comments should not explain \"what\" code does, they explain \"why\" (or perhaps \"how\" in a clever-but-difficult implementation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:46
#: 202495d70e6242ea851ec9c6d7fb40dc
msgid "Resist moving code within files/libraries. Preserving the in-file location of code is preferred over rearranging the file(s) to improve organization. Defer to a reviewer's judgement to resolve any disagreements regarding this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:51
#: 5521c01b181345b69bc8cef29bf52c1b
msgid "Do not clean up whitespace, unless you are already changing the lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:53
#: 969b9fc8212f4cb9b263d85db3234550
msgid "**Well-written, concise comments** are encouraged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:55
#: de29fe6ba5d64dd1ba03587d2248e59b
msgid "Commit messages should be of the form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:63
#: 2af081a5866a453a9c31c25e55c03765
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:71
#: 6f701a6e8ad94e3487e2106f6c8e8c7e
msgid "The brief description (summary) line should be less than 72 characters so it renders correctly in Github."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:73
#: c44304ddd926431a8b94d5b18814306b
msgid "**clean up your local commit history** :ref:`using interactive rebase <git-interactive-rebase>` (i.e. ``git rebase -i \"HEAD~10\"``) to re-arrange patches and fold things together. The idea is to present a logical set of patches for review. It can take a bit of effort to get used to interactive rebase, but it is definitely worth learning. Refer to `online resources <http://gitready.com/advanced/2009/02/10/squashing-commits-with-rebase.html>`__ to understand how to use this tool. Also see this video: https://youtu.be/iMUWQUD_Rsg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:80
#: 3d2da793e05a4a74a415bbcb3b422573
msgid "Each commit should involve only a single library. The commits of the changes in each library should be squashed (see :ref:`git-interactive-rebase`) into the minimal number of commits per library that allows readability and clarity when reviewing (usually only one commit). The \"Tools/gittools/git-subsystems-split\" script can be run on any commit spanning multiple libraries to create a single commit for each library module affected before submitting. if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:82
#: b810193728384427a8f0f02c9a29979a
msgid "Do not submit patches with commented-out code or code that is never reachable within ``#define`` s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:84
#: 4cf0b6353ed24bfe96a606b6a06cdc3f
msgid "Do not include git merge commits in your commit history; :ref:`rebase <git-rebase>`  your branch on the master branch, do not ``git pull`` changes in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:86
#: 8408c81100194b94a3e91fc3d6164fd6
msgid "Do not include any git ``fixup!`` commits in your PR; these are only ever supposed to be a temporary part of a git workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:88
#: 02bba1b5fdd146e7a571bdd1acc74837
msgid "Try to follow the :ref:`style guide <style-guide>` so your code fits in with the existing code. In particular, ensure your editor uses 4 spaces instead of tabs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:91
#: a991fad8e4314c22aba51eba32edb731
msgid "For Python changes follow the :ref:`style guide <python-style-guide>` so your code fits in with the existing code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:93
#: 630c3cb043854b41a68b06652fea7b37
msgid "Unix line endings (LF) are used. Git should take care of this automatically, but if you notice that you have a lot of files that show up as changed in ``git status`` but you didn't touch those files, you may need to `check to see if local git settings regarding line endings are correct <https://help.github.com/articles/dealing-with-line-endings>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:99
#: 390c759773bc4e859d165644cae85b58
msgid "read your changes, doing your own review. The best way to do this is to use the \"gitk\" tool. Look over your own changes critically. Make sure they do not include anything you don't want to go into the pull request. It is best to read your changes at least several hours after you wrote the code, and preferably the next day. Look over them carefully and look for any bugs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:106
#: e0049a66faa64d2f96b29b29a391ca66
msgid "if you have access to a Linux build environment then build your modified tree using `Tools/scripts/build_all.sh <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/scripts/build_all.sh>`__. That will test that all the builds for different boards and vehicle types work. If you don't have a Linux build environment then please test the build for Pixhawk boards and rover, copter and plane if your changes may affect those vehicles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:114
#: dfc69fe8dd494e0c9e5c88d9b5a9f053
msgid "test your changes in :ref:`SITL <sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop>` if possible. If you can't run SITL then test your changes in a real vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:118
#: 6dbd668aa12942d7aa423da5a85413a8
msgid "Submitting a pull request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:120
#: ce2425975de94f1cab41a4507b5dcf39
msgid "To submit a `pull request on GitHub <https://help.github.com/articles/using-pull-requests>`__ for review and possible inclusion in the official repository, follow these directions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:123
#: 41f8a68b02204387affa7dec0dbbd5c7
msgid "Open your :ref:`fork <git-fork>` on the GitHub web page select the branch from the drop-down and then push the \"New Pull Request\" button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:129
#: 8c44aa87efaf4e019c9e91ccef78f838
msgid "Check the \"base fork\" is `ArduPilot/ardupilot <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot>`__ and \"base\" is \"master\" and then fill in the PR's subject line and detailed description.  The detailed description should include any evidence of testing performed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:131
#: d8a926e1204b4546843c850ccc66e57f
msgid "Check the list of changes at the bottom of the page only includes your intended changes, then push the \"Create pull request\" button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:139
#: f405b70e498143bcb3f4bd9d177f9b0f
msgid "Next Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:141
#: a74dc428668340eabc517c56382108d8
msgid "You can track the state of your PR from the `Pull Requests list <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/pulls>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:143
#: 2fae9785c1bf4e37b15437948731832b
msgid "PRs are more likely to be merged quickly if:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:145
#: 7756c1013d1d4bfd942f90778aa29081
msgid "The PR clearly states what changes in behaviour are expected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:146
#: fa6361b581a54bd0b4f3d6ec4599073f
msgid "Good testing evidence is provided.  This could be graphs of logs recorded before and after the change, possibly from a :ref:`simulation <simulation-2>`. Check for existing :ref:`autotests <the-ardupilot-autotest-framework>`, and update them if they get broken by the change. Add new ones to cover new functionality you're introducing, or bug fixes presently not tested, if you are capable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:147
#: 21ab2d87fda14b00a685670c336b3285
msgid "Code follows the :ref:`style guide <style-guide>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:148
#: 075cdf2eebd745c78d927a1336698f2c
msgid "Python code follows the :ref:`python style guide <python-style-guide>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:149
#: 8f94aef112c44b19b5d283ac9993691c
msgid "Each commit in the PR affects only one subsystem and the commit title is prefixed with the subsystem name (e.g. \"AP_GPS: correct uBlox logging parameter descriptions\").  The `Tools/gittools/git-subsystems-split <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/gittools/git-subsystems-split>`__ script may be useful for this"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:150
#: 4cefbb549d664021b5a2cabd7d2de751
msgid "PR passes all automated CI tests.  CI tests sometimes fail for reason unrelated to your PR (e.g. dependency failures, \"flapping tests\").  Please force push the PR to re-run the tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:151
#: 81328f494d634e09966414de22db3ef8
msgid "The PR is discussed on one of the :ref:`weekly dev calls <ardupilot-discord-server>`.  To get the PR discussed add the \"DevCallTopic\" or \"DevCallEU\" label.  If you are unable to add the label ping one of the core developers on `ArduPilot Discord <https://ardupilot.org/discord>`__ (see the \"code-review\" channel).  \"Core developers\" can be identified by the \"dev-team\" badge in Discord and some also appear as `top contributors in Github <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/graphs/contributors>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:153
#: 8d7bf7cfd7d24a749f5861af0e3ca859
msgid "It is very common, especially for large changes, for the core developers to ask you to modify the pull request to fit in better with the existing code base or resolve some knock-on impact that you may not have known about. Please don't take this the wrong way, we're definitely not trying to make your life difficult!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:155
#: 08517baf8df345d38e29e1a33a0e4172
msgid "If your PR gets stuck please understand that this is likely just because ArduPilot receives a lot of code contributions and it is difficult for the core dev team to review and merge them all.  Here's some advice to get a PR \"unstuck\":"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:157
#: fff1d6ce280e41f99e788c06eed5c82f
msgid "Review the advice above titled \"PRs are more likely to be merged quickly if\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:158
#: a468d2edca8d447cadcf33a6fb85b124
msgid "Attend one of the two :ref:`weekly dev calls <ardupilot-discord-server>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/submitting-patches-back-to-master.rst:159
#: 306e1ca5cd9e48109e0d90cc4f011128
msgid "Send a note to a \"core developer\" in the code-review channel.  These can be identified by the \"dev-team\" badge in Discord and some also appear as `top contributors in Github <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/graphs/contributors>`__"
msgstr ""
